# Define the projects this benchmark will scan + query against.
# Pick 3+ projects that span a meaningful gradient (size, language, familiarity)
# to surface real cross-project signal rather than per-codebase quirk.
#
# Each entry needs:
#   key:    short stable identifier used in CSV output
#   path:   absolute path to the project root
#   notes:  free-text for your own bookkeeping (size hint, language, role)

targets:
  - key: target_a
    path: /absolute/path/to/small-python-project
    notes: |
      Small (~10 dirs), Python, project you wrote — control case where
      everything fits in head. README_AI.md should NOT change much vs source-only.
  - key: target_b
    path: /absolute/path/to/medium-python-project
    notes: |
      Medium (~50 dirs), Python, real working codebase. The "I touch this
      weekly" case. README_AI.md helping or not should matter here.
  - key: target_c
    path: /absolute/path/to/large-legacy-codebase
    notes: |
      Large (100+ dirs), language other than Python or unfamiliar to you.
      The "I would have to explore from scratch" case. Where the navigation
      story for README_AI.md SHOULD pay off the most.
